From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:27:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] EXPERIMENT (not for main): mutable_array::probe_linear, a
 probe primitive

The runtime-primitive experiment of the hash-table milestone
(HASH-TABLE-EXPERIMENT.md, "Runtime experiments";
HASH-TABLE-COMPILER-PRESSURE.md, RT-1): the whole linear probing walk of
a table of stored hashes (negative = empty) and keys as one runtime
operation, mutable_array::probe_linear(hashes, keys, h, key), returning
the slot of KEY or -1 - I for the empty slot I ending its sequence.

* core/mutarray.tcl: the Tcl implementation (interp, compile) and the
  registration (observe ownership, structural equality, IndexNotFound
  when a slot is outside KEYS);
* native: NIR op mutarrayprobe, Rust rt_mutarray_probe (no allocation,
  no safepoint; fallible through ==), its helper symbol;
* audit/hash-table/impl/lpp.bot: lpa with find_from/empty_from replaced
  by the primitive (fuzzed on four backends, 144 checks, 0 failures).

The policy, layout, growth and deletion stay Botlish. This branch exists
to measure the primitive; it is not proposed as an intrinsic.

